le","messageStrings":{"issue":{"text":"Focus isn't showing"}},"properties":{"howToFix":["Change the FocusedBorderThickness property to be more than 0."],"whyFix":"If the focus isn't visible, people who don't use a mouse won't be able to see it when they're interacting with the app.","level":"Medium","componentType":"app","primaryCategory":"accessibility"}},{"id":"acc-TabIndexShouldBeDefinedForInteractiveControl","messageStrings":{"issue":{"text":"Missing tab stop"}},"properties":{"howToFix":["Set TabIndex to 0 or greater to ensure that interactive elements have a tab stop."],"whyFix":"People who use the keyboard with your app will not be able to access this element without a tab stop.","level":"Medium","componentType":"app","primaryCategory":"accessibility"}},{"id":"acc-AccessibleLabelNeeded","messageStrings":{"issue":{"text":"Missing accessible label"}},"properties":{"howToFix":["Edit the accessible label property to describe the item."],"whyFix":"If there's no accessible text, people who can’t see the screen won't understand what’s in images and controls.","level":"Medium","componentType":"app","primaryCategory":"accessibility"}},{"id":"app-CollectingReadOnlyTable","messageStrings":{"issue":{"text":"Collection is initialized but never updated"}},"properties":{"howToFix":["Replace the Collect or ClearCollect with a named formula on App.Formulas. For example, MyTable = Filter(source, condition). Named formulas are computed when their inputs change and do not carry the tracking cost of a collection."],"whyFix":"Collections are meant to be updated. Power Apps does extra work to keep track of every collection so that anything depending on it stays in sync when the data changes. When the data never changes after it is set, that tracking work is wasted. A named formula gives the same data without the extra cost.","componentType":"app","primaryCategory":"performance","level":"Medium"}},{"id":"app-CrossScreenEventDependencies","messageStrings":{"issue":{"text":"Event rule references a control on another screen"}},"properties":{"howToFix":["Move the work to an event on the owning screen (for example, Screen.OnVisible), or pass state between screens using Navigate's context parameter or a global variable and react to it on the target screen."],"whyFix":"Event rules (such as OnStart, OnVisible, and OnSelect) that reference controls on other screens force those screens to load and initialize early, even if the user never navigates to them. This can noticeably slow app start-up and navigation.","componentType":"app","primaryCategory":"performance","level":"Medium"}}]}},"invocations":[{"executionSuccessful":true}],"columnKind":"utf16CodeUnits"}]}